# ── Optional: AI-assisted study (recommended) ────────────────────────────────
# When set, picking a question uses Claude to select the most relevant gospel
# topics, write a short neutral framing, and suggest extra REAL scripture
# references (every reference is validated against the full scriptures dataset,
# so a made-up verse can never appear). Without this key the app still works
# using keyword matching over the built-in topical index.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: shared multi-device sessions (recommended for a live class) ─────
# For everyone to submit and vote from their own phones, the app needs a shared
# store. The easiest path on Vercel: Storage tab → create an Upstash Redis (or
# KV) store and "Connect" it to this project. Vercel injects these automatically
# — you don't have to paste anything. To run it yourself, create a free Upstash
# Redis database (https://upstash.com) and copy its REST URL + token here.
#
# The app accepts either the Upstash names or the Vercel KV names:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#
# Without any of these, the app runs in single-screen mode (one device, e.g. a
# laptop passed around or projected) — great for testing, but phones won't sync.
